      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Blackbanks, Howth Road, Raheny is a particularly scenic and sought-after coastal location. Properties situated on the seaward side of Howth Road benefit from an elevated position, with spectacular south-facing views extending across Bull Island Nature Reserve and Dublin Bay, with the city skyline and Dublin Mountains providing a stunning backdrop.\r\n\r\nNumber 643B is an attractive, modern detached family home, ideally positioned along this highly regarded stretch of Howth Road. Extending to approximately 223 sq. m., this impressive property offers generous, well-proportioned accommodation together with an abundance of natural light and, most notably, spectacular views from the rear of the house.\r\n\r\nOn entering, a welcoming porch leads into a bright and spacious reception hallway. To the front is a well-proportioned living room featuring a bay window, while a guest WC is conveniently located off the hallway.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the heart of the home is undoubtedly the impressive open-plan kitchen and dining area, which enjoys an excellent sense of space and direct access through patio doors to the rear garden. The kitchen flows seamlessly into a beautiful family/sunroom area, positioned to take full advantage of the magnificent views. This is a wonderful space for family gatherings, relaxing and entertaining, and is sure to be one of the most enjoyed rooms in the house. A separate utility room, with access to the side of the property, completes the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, a generous landing provides access to four bedrooms. Two of the bedrooms benefit from ensuite shower rooms, while the principal bedroom, located to the rear, is further enhanced by a walk-in dressing room and enjoys the spectacular views across Bull Island and Dublin Bay. A second bedroom also benefits from these wonderful views.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property is approached via a gravelled driveway with a separate gated pedestrian entrance. The front entrance area is paved and provides an attractive approach to the house.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is a particularly special feature of the property. A large paved patio provides an excellent space for outdoor dining and entertaining, while a mature hedge offers privacy and shelter. Beyond the patio, a generous lawn extends towards the rear boundary, allowing the stunning outlook to take centre stage.\r\n\r\nThe location is exceptional, with all the amenities of Raheny Village within easy reach. There is an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools nearby, while the coastal promenade and scenic walks along the seafront are quite literally on the doorstep. The magnificent St. Anne’s Park is also close by, providing extensive parkland, gardens and recreational facilities. Excellent transport links further enhance the appeal of this highly sought-after address, with Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas readily accessible.\r\n\r\n643B Howth Road represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial, modern detached family home in one of Raheny’s most desirable coastal settings. The combination of generous accommodation, superb gardens, excellent amenities and, above all, the breathtaking south-facing views makes this a truly special home.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the exceptional setting and everything this fine property has to offer."
      },
